codex
A concrete deploy/config issue is emerging: the Sushi policy normalizer validates each allowlist independently, but unlike LI.FI it does not require selector entries to cover exactly the configured call targets. That can pass deploy-time reconciliation while leaving the registered Sushi taker unable to execute routes. I’m checking tests and route execution code to make sure this is not already rejected elsewhere before I promote it.
